<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Apple's privacy manifest. Hand-maintained, and NOT generated by xcodegen the
	way Info.plist is — `project.yml` describes the target's Info.plist only. It
	reaches the bundle because the ICSApp target takes `sources: - path: ics_ios`
	and excludes nothing but Info.plist, so this file is copied as a resource.

	Two separate obligations are answered here.

	1. Required-reason APIs. An upload that touches one without declaring it comes
	   back from App Store Connect as ITMS-91053, "Missing API declaration". This
	   app touches exactly one, NSUserDefaults, in DiscordSession.ios.kt: the
	   install marker whose whole point is to have the opposite lifetime to the
	   Keychain, so a reinstall purges a session the previous owner of the device
	   left behind. CA92.1 is the matching reason — the app reads and writes only
	   its own data, in its own container.

	   PreviewFrameEngine.ios.kt is the other file that touches the file system,
	   but only through URLsForDirectory, createDirectoryAtURL and
	   fileExistsAtPath, none of which are required-reason APIs. If either file
	   grows a new call — disk space, file timestamps, system boot time — this
	   list grows with it or the next upload bounces.

	2. Tracking and collection, in machine-readable form. Both are empty because
	   both are actually empty: no analytics, crash reporting or advertising SDK
	   is embedded, and nothing about the user is transmitted and retained. This
	   has to agree with the App Privacy answers in App Store Connect and with
	   docs/privacy/index.html — see docs/app-store-release-notes.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
